/-! ## §5. THE SIX FACTS

Stated in exactly the shape `Zeta2SupScheme.routeB_ingredients` and
`Zeta2L7Assembly.routeB_l7_rate` take them (LEAN.md §3: state a lemma with exactly the
hypotheses its caller produces).  §6 makes the kernel check that. -/

/-- (1) **Left bracket sign.**  `0 ≤ g'(w* - r)` — EXACT: `R(w*-r) < 0` is a rational
fact, so this carries no enclosure error at all. -/
theorem c7_hbl : (0 : ℝ) ≤ Zeta2SupScheme.phaseD Finset.univ Zeta2SupScheme.qB
    (26 - Zeta2SupScheme.sigT) 1 (wsB - rB) := by
  rw [phaseD_wsm, neg_nonneg, Real.arctan_le_zero]
  norm_num

/-- (2) **Right bracket sign.**  `g'(w* + r) ≤ 0` — EXACT, same reason. -/
theorem c7_hbr : Zeta2SupScheme.phaseD Finset.univ Zeta2SupScheme.qB
    (26 - Zeta2SupScheme.sigT) 1 (wsB + rB) ≤ 0 := by
  rw [phaseD_wsp, neg_nonpos, Real.arctan_nonneg]
  norm_num

/-- (3) **`|g'(w*)| ≤ ε`** at C6's certified `ε = 10⁻⁹`. -/
theorem c7_heps : |Zeta2SupScheme.phaseD Finset.univ Zeta2SupScheme.qB
